\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Mean service day per zone for CFA under centrality-based (left) and value-based (right) zone selection, averaged over 500 runs. Green = serviced early, red = serviced late. Under centrality, the service order is strictly concentric, with zones near the depot always visited first and outer zones last. Value-based selection breaks this pattern, pulling economically critical zones forward to early service days regardless of geographic distance from the depot.\relax }}{44}{figure.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:zone_maps}{{7}{44}{Mean service day per zone for CFA under centrality-based (left) and value-based (right) zone selection, averaged over 500 runs. Green = serviced early, red = serviced late. Under centrality, the service order is strictly concentric, with zones near the depot always visited first and outer zones last. Value-based selection breaks this pattern, pulling economically critical zones forward to early service days regardless of geographic distance from the depot.\relax }{figure.caption.9}{}}
